--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Graph / Build / Objects: group and sort by usage
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Context:
The user asked to also sort and group the Objects tab by usage, the way the
Cache tab names its companion tables. Grouping by source (backend) stays
available through a toggle.

Changes:
1. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/BuildObjects.py
   - New usage_of(name) classifier and USAGES order: Graph data, Inferred,
     Search cache, Simulations, Analytics. Every item is tagged with its usage
     in _group(); the response gains `usages` (ordered keys and titles).
2. src/front/templates/partials/dtwin/_build_objects.html
   - "By usage" / "By source" toggle in the filter bar; By usage is the default.
3. src/front/static/query/js/query-build-objects.js
   - By-usage view: one block per bucket, rows sorted by kind (views, tables,
     registrations) then name, each row showing its source. Failed sections stay
     visible on top. Delete all keeps the drop-safe source order in both views.
4. docs/user-guide.md
   - Describes the usage grouping and the toggle.
5. tests/units/dtwin/test_build_objects.py,
   tests/units/front/test_build_objects_tab_contract.py
   - usage_of cases, usage tags and view-first ordering on Postgres objects,
     usages order in the response, toggle default and usage-view wiring.

